        "original_id": "95714122-2aed-5d5d-818f-22f7a963b5db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeremy Brock, Kevin Macdonald, Channing Tatum, Jamie Bell, Donald Sutherland, Rosemary Sutcliff, Alexandros Avranas\n- Works: The Eagle, The Eagle of the Ninth, True Crimes, Mrs Brown, Driving Lessons, The Last King of Scotland, Charlotte Gray\n- Topics: screenwriting, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Rosemary Sutcliff wrote the historical adventure novel \"The Eagle of the Ninth\" in 1954.\n- Jeremy Brock, born in 1959, is an English writer and director and was appointed MBE.\n- Jeremy Brock's works include the screenplays \"Mrs Brown,\" \"Driving Lessons,\" \"The Last King of Scotland,\" \"Charlotte Gray,\" and \"The Eagle.\"\n- \"The Eagle\" is a 2011 epic historical drama film set in Roman Britain.\n- Kevin Macdonald directed \"The Eagle,\" and the film stars Channing Tatum, Jamie Bell, and Donald Sutherland.\n- Jeremy Brock adapted \"The Eagle\" from Rosemary Sutcliff's 1954 novel \"The Eagle of the Ninth.\"\n- \"The Eagle\" tells the story of a young Roman officer searching northern Great Britain for the lost eagle standard of his father's legion.\n- \"True Crimes\" is a 2016 American-Polish crime drama-thriller film directed by Alexandros Avranas and written by Jeremy Brock.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
